#!/bin/sh
# Configure the TAYGA tunnel and its explicit routes for the selected WAN
# profile. This helper is intentionally limited to the well-known NAT64 prefix
# and the dedicated dynamic IPv4 pool; it never creates a client IPv4 gateway
# or a broad route.
set -eu

. /usr/lib/lanrith/network-profile.sh
. /usr/lib/lanrith/network-checks.sh

interface=$lanrith_nat64_interface

remove() {
  if ip link show dev "$interface" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    require_translation_tun "$interface" || return 1
  fi
  ip -6 route del "$lanrith_nat64_prefix" dev "$interface" 2>/dev/null || true
  ip route del "$lanrith_nat64_ipv4_pool" dev "$interface" 2>/dev/null || true
  if ip link show dev "$interface" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    ip link set "$interface" down 2>/dev/null || true
    tayga --rmtun --config /etc/tayga.conf 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
}

if [ "${1:-}" = remove ]; then
  [ "$#" -eq 1 ] || { echo 'Usage: configure-nat64 [remove]' >&2; exit 64; }
  remove
  exit 0
fi
[ "$#" -eq 0 ] || { echo 'Usage: configure-nat64 [remove]' >&2; exit 64; }
[ "$lanrith_nat64_enabled" = 1 ] || {
  echo 'NAT64 is not enabled in the signed profile.' >&2
  exit 1
}

if ! ip link show dev "$interface" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  tayga --mktun --config /etc/tayga.conf
fi
require_translation_tun "$interface" || { echo 'Refusing a non-TUN NAT64 interface.' >&2; exit 1; }
ip link set "$interface" up
# Reconcile an interrupted pre-start or an older prefix length on this TUN.
# Service/transit routes are on other interfaces and are never flushed here.
ip -4 address flush dev "$interface" scope global
ip -4 route flush dev "$interface"
ip address replace "$lanrith_nat64_ipv4_cidr" dev "$interface"
ip -6 address replace "$lanrith_nat64_ipv6_cidr" dev "$interface"
ip route replace "$lanrith_nat64_ipv4_pool" dev "$interface"
ip -6 route replace "$lanrith_nat64_prefix" dev "$interface"
